INT. CASTELLANO'S LAUNDRY & DRY CLEANING - BACK ROOM - NIGHT

Steam. Rows of plastic-wrapped suits. A pressing machine hisses.

VINCE CASTELLANO, 50s, in an undershirt, stands over a table of cash. DOLLY, 40s, in a pressed blouse, folds a sheet with great care. MOE ZIELINSKI, 60s, a hulking presser, sets down the iron. NADIA, 20s, new to the shop, feeds a collar into the machine.

Vince counts. Dolly folds. Nobody speaks.

Nadia glances at the door.

VINCE
Moe.

MOE
Yeah?

VINCE
Whose turn was it to lock up?

MOE
(together with Dolly)
Mine.

^DOLLY
Hers.

They look at each other. Dolly's fold goes crooked.

VINCE
Which?

MOE
I locked it.

DOLLY
I saw him. He locked it.

Vince sets down the cash. Nadia presses the machine. It hisses. Steam hides her face.

VINCE
(to Nadia)
Kid, you got somewhere to be?

NADIA
No, sir.

VINCE
You keep looking at that door.

Nadia lets go of the machine. A beat. Moe picks up the iron again. Behind her, the front bell chimes.
